## 📱 SIM and Phone Example (Tight vs Loose Coupling)

# Tight Coupling Example (Fixed SIM Phone)

Imagine a phone that works with **only one specific SIM card permanently fixed inside it**.

## Scenario:

- Phone is built to work only with “Airtel SIM”
- SIM is inside the phone and cannot be changed

## Code analogy:

```java id="t2"
class AirtelSim {
    void network() {
        System.out.println("Airtel network connected");
    }
}

class Phone {
    AirtelSim sim = new AirtelSim(); // tightly coupled

    void call() {
        sim.network();
        System.out.println("Calling...");
    }
}
```

---

## Problem:

- You cannot use Jio or Vi SIM
- If Airtel changes its implementation, phone must change
- Very rigid system

This is **TIGHT COUPLING**

---

## Real-life meaning:

A phone locked to one SIM = no flexibility

---

# Loose Coupling Example (Normal Smartphone)

Now imagine a modern smartphone:

✔ You can insert any SIM (Jio / Airtel / Vi)
✔ You can remove and replace SIM anytime
✔ Phone does not care which SIM is used

---

## Code analogy using interface:

```java id="t3"
interface Sim {
    void network();
}
```

```java id="t4"
class JioSim implements Sim {
    public void network() {
        System.out.println("Jio network connected");
    }
}
```

```java id="t5"
class AirtelSim implements Sim {
    public void network() {
        System.out.println("Airtel network connected");
    }
}
```

```java id="t6"
class Phone {
    private Sim sim;

    // SIM is inserted (Dependency Injection)
    Phone(Sim sim) {
        this.sim = sim;
    }

    void call() {
        sim.network();
        System.out.println("Calling...");
    }
}
```

---

## Usage:

```java id="t7"
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Sim sim1 = new JioSim();
        Phone phone1 = new Phone(sim1);
        phone1.call();

        Sim sim2 = new AirtelSim();
        Phone phone2 = new Phone(sim2);
        phone2.call();
    }
}
```

---

# Why this is Loose Coupling?

- Phone does NOT depend on a specific SIM
- Any SIM can be used
- Easy to change without modifying phone code
- Flexible and scalable

---

# Quick Comparison (SIM Example)

| Feature       | Tight Coupling      | Loose Coupling          |
| ------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------- |
| SIM usage     | Fixed (Airtel only) | Any SIM (Jio/Airtel/Vi) |
| Flexibility   | Low                 | High                    |
| Change impact | High                | Low                     |
| Design        | Rigid               | Flexible                |
